---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Page
  title="Findings — Aethens"
  description="Published findings on Terminal-Bench 2 and SWE-bench Verified. Each was confirmed with the benchmark's own harness."
>
  <article class="wrap py-16 sm:py-20 max-w-3xl">
    <p class="kicker mb-5"><span>Findings</span></p>
    <h1 class="font-serif italic font-semibold text-section leading-[1.1]">
      What we reported, after checking it with their harness.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-paper/90">
      These notes name defects in other people’s benchmarks. The Terminal-Bench 2 converter and the
      SWE-bench patch probes that surfaced them are not part of the v0.1.0 release. Each result was
      confirmed with that benchmark’s own harness, not with Aethens’ grader. The policy for findings
      that are not yet public is
      <a class="prose-link" href="https://github.com/beastrog/aethens/blob/main/docs/DISCLOSURE.md">docs/DISCLOSURE.md</a>.
      Harness commands, and what is not in the repository, are in
      <a class="prose-link" href="https://github.com/beastrog/aethens/blob/main/docs/reproduce-findings.md">docs/reproduce-findings.md</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="terminal-bench-2" class="mt-14 font-serif italic text-3xl">Terminal-Bench 2</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
      A broken solution scored full reward: 3 of 3 tests passed, reward 1. Confirmed with
      Terminal-Bench’s own harness.
    </p>

    <h2 id="swe-bench" class="mt-14 font-serif italic text-3xl">SWE-bench Verified</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
      Wrong patches were graded resolved on 9 instances: 8 test gaps across 4 repositories
      (sphinx-doc, astropy, django, and pydata/xarray), plus a log-parser bug on
      <code class="text-gold">sympy__sympy-14248</code>.
      <code class="text-gold">parse_log_sympy</code> keys results by bare test name, so a later file
      that shares the name can leave a failing test recorded as passed. Reported to the SWE-bench
      maintainers in
      <a class="prose-link" href="https://github.com/SWE-bench/SWE-bench/issues/733">issue #733</a>.
      Confirmed with <code class="text-gold">swebench.harness.run_evaluation</code> from swebench 5.0.2.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
      <code class="text-gold">django__django-16631</code> is one of those test gaps. The instance
      tests do not check that a password change logs the user out, so a patch that leaves the
      session authenticated is graded resolved. That is a gap in the instance tests, not a Django
      security issue.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">
      The same page on the repository README is the text source for this note.
      Bench precision and recall, which measure Aethens itself, are on the
      <a class="prose-link" href={`${base}accuracy/`}>accuracy page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Page>
